DRIVERS                                                        [3.0]
-------

Format:      DRIVERS

Purpose:     Displays information about the disk drivers present  in
        the system.

Use:         For every disk driver: its name and version (or  'Legacy
        MSX-DOS driver' for drivers that are not  Nextor  ones),  the
        slot it lives in (with the RAM segment after a  colon,   when
        the driver is loaded in RAM) and the range of  drive  letters
        that were assigned to it at boot time.

             The same function is provided by the DRIVERS.COM  exter-
        nal tool, which also works on older Nextor versions.

Examples:

        DRIVERS
        Nextor internal SD driver v1.2 on slot 2
        Drives assigned at boot time: 2, from A: to B:

        Turbo-R FDD v3.0 on slot 3-2:4
        Drives assigned at boot time: 1, C:

             Two drivers are present: one in  the  ROM  of  slot   2,
        with drives A: and B:,  and one loaded in RAM segment 4  with
        its master slot being 3-2, with drive C:.
